course: dictionary
lesson: 2160
title: The cornea, the clear front of the eye
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The cornea is the clear, curved layer at the front of your eye. It covers the iris and the pupil, so it is the part you see when you look at someone's eyes. Its job is to help focus light.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «Organ donation means giving healthy organs, such as the heart, kidneys, liver, lungs or corneas (the clear front of the eye)...» The bracket tells you what corneas are, and words like clear and front are clues.
explain: In science, the order matters. Light reaches the cornea first, which bends it, then the lens finishes focusing it on the retina at the back of the eye. Say the path out loud: cornea, lens, retina.
fact: The cornea is the clear, curved, dome-shaped layer at the front of the eye.
fact: The cornea covers the iris and the pupil.
fact: The cornea bends light first, and then the lens finishes focusing it.
fact: Goggles protect the cornea from chemicals and flying bits.
fact: A scratch on the cornea hurts a lot. Some people receive a donated cornea in a transplant.
exercise: What is the cornea? | The coloured part of the eye | *The clear, curved layer at the front of the eye | A bone in the skull | The nerve that carries messages to the brain
exercise: Which part of the eye bends light first? | The optic nerve | *The cornea | The retina | The lens
exercise: Which protects the cornea from chemicals and flying bits? | A plaster | A helmet | *Goggles | Gloves
test: Which layer covers the iris and the pupil? | The kidneys | *The cornea | The retina | The optic nerve
test: Which part does light reach first, the cornea or the lens? | *The cornea | The retina | The optic nerve | The lens
exam: What does the bracket in «corneas (the clear front of the eye)» tell you? | It says corneas are a type of heart | It shows corneas only belong to animals | *It explains what corneas are | It is a mistake and can be ignored
